NAME
       init - switch the run level (old System V interface to systemd)

SYNOPSIS
       init RUNLEVEL

DESCRIPTION
       On RHEL 9 the first process (PID 1) is systemd; /sbin/init is a link to
       it. Typed by root as a command, "init N" is kept for old habits and asks
       systemd to switch to the target that matches the old run level N:

       0        poweroff.target (switch off)
       1, s, S  rescue.target (single user)
       2, 3, 4  multi-user.target (text console, network)
       5        graphical.target (graphical login)
       6        reboot.target (restart)

       The change lasts until the next boot. The systemd way is
       "systemctl isolate multi-user.target" for now, and
       "systemctl set-default multi-user.target" for every boot.

EXAMPLES
              # init 3          (same as: systemctl isolate multi-user.target)
              # init 6          (same as: systemctl reboot)

SEE ALSO
       systemctl(1), systemd.special(7), runlevel(8), shutdown(8)
